{"name":"White Primer","hex":"#c3bdab","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"white","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Bright and colourless; reflecting equal quantities of all frequencies of visible light.","Of or relating to Europeans or those of European descent, regardless if their skin has cool or warm undertones."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of snow or milk; the color of light containing equal amounts of all visible wavelengths.","A person of European descent with light-colored skin."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/white"},{"term":"primer","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A prayer or devotional book intended for laity, initially an abridgment of the breviary and manual including the hours of the Virgin Mary, 15 gradual and 7 penitential psalms, the litany, the placebo and dirige forming the office of the dead, and the commendations.","Any of various similar works issued in England for private prayer in accordance with the Book of Common Prayer."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any substance or device, such as priming wire or blasting cap, used to ignite gunpowder or other explosive.","A person who primes explosives."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/primer"}],"entries":[{"title":"Primer (paint)","blocks":[{"text":"A primer or undercoat is a preparatory coating put on materials before painting. Priming ensures better adhesion of paint to the surface, increases paint durability, and provides additional protection for the material being painted."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/White_primer_bucket.jpg/330px-White_primer_bucket.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Primer_(paint)","wikidata":"Q380866"},{"title":"White","blocks":[{"text":"White is the lightest color and is achromatic. It is the color of objects such as snow, chalk, and milk, and is the opposite of black. White objects fully reflect and scatter all the visible wavelengths of light. White on television and computer screens is created by a mixture of red, blue, and green light. The color white can be given with white pigments, especially titanium dioxide."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg/330px-Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White","wikidata":"Q23444"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Autolack_4_Grundierung_IMG_2409.JPG/500px-Autolack_4_Grundierung_IMG_2409.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Autolack_4_Grundierung_IMG_2409.JPG/500px-Autolack_4_Grundierung_IMG_2409.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Primer as a step in the coating process of a car body.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAutolack_4_Grundierung_IMG_2409.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a1/Zinc_chromate_primer.jpg/500px-Zinc_chromate_primer.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a1/Zinc_chromate_primer.jpg/1280px-Zinc_chromate_primer.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a1/Zinc_chromate_primer.jpg/500px-Zinc_chromate_primer.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Zinc chromate primer","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AZinc_chromate_primer.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Canonization_2014-The_Canonization_of_Saint_John_XXIII_and_Saint_John_Paul_II_%2814037015405%29.jpg/500px-Canonization_2014-The_Canoniz